Trees, with species and dimensions (Urban Forest)
-------------------------------------------------

Dataset: trees (82,064 trees the City of Melbourne maintains, one point
each)

Publisher: the City of Melbourne, on its open data portal, the dataset
"Trees, with species and dimensions (Urban Forest)", updated on
2025-09-22.
https://data.melbourne.vic.gov.au/explore/dataset/trees-with-species-and-dimensions-urban-forest/

Licence: Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International (CC-BY-4.0), as
the dataset's catalogue record states it ("CC BY", with the licence's
address https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/legalcode).

Credit: City of Melbourne Open Data.

Where and when: read on 2026-10-12 from the portal's own interface:

  https://data.melbourne.vic.gov.au/api/explore/v2.1/catalog/datasets/trees-with-species-and-dimensions-urban-forest
  (the catalogue record: licence, update time, record count)
  https://data.melbourne.vic.gov.au/api/explore/v2.1/catalog/datasets/trees-with-species-and-dimensions-urban-forest/exports/parquet
  (the whole dataset, 6,820,296 bytes, SHA-256 b86b1e1db12f0146a35a48ea55fce4971f9fcc5b4244abe9fcfcbf1ad2893289)

Kept: for each tree, its id, common and scientific name, genus, family,
whether it stands in a street or a park, its precinct, its age class and
its useful life expectancy class, with the class's upper end in years
(under 10 years as 10, over 41 years as 50); its place from the dataset's
longitude and latitude. A tree whose useful life class is empty is marked
"Not assessed" and given no years, though the export carries 50 for it.
The class names are reworded ("< 10 years" as "Under 10 years", "11 - 20
years" as "11 to 20 years", "> 41 years" as "Over 40 years"). Left out:
the trunk diameter (missing for most trees, impossible for some), the
planting year and date (1900 stands in for a third of the trees), the
upload date and the eastings and northings. This is a modified version of
the dataset.


